---
import CallToAction from "../components/CallToAction.astro";
import Container from "../components/Container.astro";
import Footer from "../components/Footer.astro";
import Nav from "../components/Nav.astro";
import Layout from "../layouts/Layout.astro";
---

<Layout
  title="Terms of Use (EULA) – Finon"
  description="Terms of Use and End User License Agreement for the Finon app, operated by Finon Ltd."
>
  <Nav />
  <main>
    <Container class="flex flex-col gap-2 py-32">
      <h1 class="font-bold text-4xl">Terms of Use (EULA)</h1>
      <p>Last updated: June 20, 2026</p>
      <p>
        These Terms of Use ("Terms") form a legally binding agreement between you
        and Finon Ltd ("Finon", "we", "us", or "our") governing your access to and
        use of the Finon mobile application and related services (together, the
        "Service"). They also serve as the End User License Agreement (EULA) for
        the Service.
      </p>

      <p>
        Please read these Terms carefully. By downloading, accessing, or using the
        Service, you confirm that you have read, understood, and agree to be bound
        by these Terms and by our <a href="https://www.finon.app/privacy"
          >Privacy Policy</a
        >. If you do not agree, do not download or use the Service.
      </p>

      <h2 class="font-bold text-2xl">Eligibility</h2>
      <p>
        You must be at least 18 years old and able to form a legally binding
        contract to use the Service. By using the Service, you represent and
        warrant that you meet these requirements. The Service is intended for
        personal, non-commercial use.
      </p>

      <h2 class="font-bold text-2xl">The Service</h2>
      <p>
        Finon is a financial dashboard that lets you connect your bank, brokerage,
        and cryptocurrency accounts to view and track your portfolio in one place.
        Connections are made through third-party account-connection providers on a
        read-only basis, which means Finon is designed to view your account
        information and cannot move, transfer, or transact with your funds.
      </p>
      <p>
        <strong>Not financial advice.</strong> The Service provides information, aggregation,
        and analytical tools for your personal use only. It does not constitute financial,
        investment, tax, legal, or other professional advice, and nothing in the Service
        is a recommendation to buy, sell, or hold any asset. You are solely responsible
        for your financial decisions. Account balances, valuations, and other figures
        are provided for convenience, may be delayed or inaccurate, and should be verified
        with your financial institution before you rely on them.
      </p>

      <h2 class="font-bold text-2xl">
        Account Connections and Third-Party Services
      </h2>
      <p>
        To use core features, you may link external financial accounts through
        third-party connection providers. Your use of those providers and of your
        financial institutions remains subject to their own terms and privacy
        practices, and we are not responsible for them. We do not control, and are
        not responsible for, the availability, accuracy, or security of any
        third-party service, and we are not liable for any loss arising from your
        use of, or reliance on, any third-party service. You authorise Finon and
        its providers to access and retrieve your account information on your
        behalf for the purpose of providing the Service.
      </p>

      <h2 class="font-bold text-2xl">Your Account and Security</h2>
      <p>
        You are responsible for maintaining the confidentiality of your login
        credentials and for all activity that occurs under your account. You agree
        to provide accurate, current, and complete information and to keep it up
        to date. Notify us immediately at <a href="mailto:support@finon.app"
          >support@finon.app</a
        > if you suspect any unauthorised use of your account or any security breach.
      </p>

      <h2 class="font-bold text-2xl">Subscriptions and Purchases</h2>
      <p>
        Some features of the Service require a paid subscription or a one-time
        purchase, sold through the Apple App Store and managed by your Apple
        Account. Finon currently offers:
      </p>

      <table>
        <thead>
          <tr><th>Plan</th><th>Type</th><th>Duration</th></tr>
        </thead>
        <tbody>
          <tr
            ><td>Monthly</td><td>Auto-renewing subscription</td><td>1 month</td
            ></tr
          >
          <tr
            ><td>Annual</td><td>Auto-renewing subscription</td><td>1 year</td></tr
          >
          <tr
            ><td>Finon Lifetime</td><td>One-time purchase (non-recurring)</td><td
              >One-time</td
            ></tr
          >
        </tbody>
      </table>

      <p>
        The title, length, and price of each plan, together with any introductory
        offer or free trial, are shown in the app and on the App Store at the
        point of purchase, in your local currency.
      </p>

      <h3 class="font-bold text-xl">Auto-renewing subscriptions</h3>
      <ul class="list-disc list-inside">
        <li>
          Payment is charged to your Apple Account at confirmation of purchase.
        </li>
        <li>
          A subscription automatically renews for the same period at the
          then-current price unless auto-renew is turned off at least 24 hours
          before the end of the current period.
        </li>
        <li>
          Your Apple Account is charged for renewal within 24 hours before the end
          of the current period.
        </li>
        <li>
          You can manage or cancel your subscription, and turn off auto-renewal,
          in your Apple Account settings after purchase.
        </li>
        <li>
          If a free trial is offered and you purchase a subscription, any unused
          portion of the free trial is forfeited.
        </li>
      </ul>

      <h3 class="font-bold text-xl">Billing grace period</h3>
      <p>
        If a renewal payment fails, eligible subscribers may keep access to paid
        features during a billing grace period of 16 days while Apple attempts to
        recover the payment. The grace period applies to eligible paid-to-paid
        renewals as determined by Apple. If payment is not recovered within the
        grace period, access to paid features ends.
      </p>

      <h3 class="font-bold text-xl">Finon Lifetime</h3>
      <p>
        Finon Lifetime is a single, one-time purchase that does not auto-renew and
        is not a subscription. It grants access to the included features for as
        long as the Service is offered, subject to these Terms.
      </p>

      <h3 class="font-bold text-xl">Price changes, cancellation, and refunds</h3>
      <p>
        We may change subscription prices from time to time. Any price change will
        apply only to renewals occurring after the change, and where required we
        will give you advance notice and the opportunity to cancel before it takes
        effect. All purchases are processed by Apple, and refund requests are
        handled by Apple in accordance with its policies; we do not directly
        process refunds for App Store purchases. You can request a refund through
        Apple's support channels.
      </p>

